<p>Hi, it&rsquo;s Pascal again. You might remember Vehicare from October: the car
maintenance log for iPhone, iPad and Mac that reads the invoice your mechanic
hands you, so you never have to type into it.</p>

<p>Your inbox is full of Black Friday sales this week. Vehicare isn&rsquo;t one of them.
Its price is the same every day: $19.99, once, for every vehicle you own, on
iPhone, iPad and Mac. No subscription, now or later.</p>

<p>You don&rsquo;t need a sale to try it, either, because the first vehicle is free. Not
a trial, and nothing that expires in 14 days: the whole app, invoice reading and
reminders included, for one car, for as long as you keep it.</p>

<p>Here&rsquo;s what that gets you this weekend:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Your glovebox, read.</strong> Share the PDF your garage emailed you, or take a
photo of the paper copy. Vehicare fills in the visit: the date, the odometer,
every job and what it cost. You check it and save.</li>
  <li><strong>What&rsquo;s due next</strong>, worked out from what was actually done and how much you
actually drive. There&rsquo;s no schedule to set up. Vehicare reminds you, or you
can ask Siri.</li>
  <li><strong>A real Mac app.</strong> Drag an invoice out of Mail onto it, sort your visits in a
table, and use it from Shortcuts.</li>
  <li><strong>Your data, in your own iCloud.</strong> No account, no analytics, no trackers. I
never see your invoices, unless you send me one it read wrong.</li>
</ul>

<p>If the car got new tires on sale this weekend, that invoice is a fine one to
start with.</p>

<p>You pay only when you want a second vehicle, PDF and CSV export, or to lose the
one small card for another indie app. It&rsquo;s the same price as last week, and it
will be the same next week.</p>

<p>It needs a device that runs Apple Intelligence: an iPhone 15 Pro or later, or an
iPad or Mac with Apple silicon, on 26.4 or later.</p>

